Gap: `path_fold`'s `path.iter().enumerate().fold(leaf, |current, (z, &sibling)| ..)` - Aeneas translates the closure, which captures the `FnMut` visitor, into `call_once` and `call_mut` instances Lean rejects (type mismatch: they return the closure's state where the trait has none)
The fold over the path is a loop over its indices, `current` the accumulator. Level `z` takes
`path[z]`, puts the running node left or right of it by bit `z` of `e`, shows the pair to `visit`
and hashes it with `node(z + 1, e >> (z + 1), ..)`: the fold's calls, in the fold's order, so the
root is the same and `visit` sees the same pairs.
Tests: path_fold_by_index_matches_the_fold, against the fold copied from the source: the root and
every pair shown, at heights 0 to 11, at indices with both values of every bit the path reads, under
a `node` that tells apart the height, the index and the order of the children.
mutation: children swapped (`== 0` -> `!= 0`) -> it fails; node index `e >> z` -> it fails; the
`visit` call dropped -> it fails.

